  "body": "Pi writes a reply's reasoning tokens on its assistant message as `usage.reasoning`, a part of `usage.output`. pi-ai's `Usage` says: \"a subset of `output`: `output` already includes these tokens\", set by providers that report a reasoning breakdown and left out by the rest. `piUsage` in `internal/sessions/pi.go` reads only `input`, `output`, `cacheRead` and `cacheWrite`, and `piCall` never sets `Call.Reasoning`, so every Pi and omp call is read with reasoning 0.\n\n`DecodeOf` checks whether a reply's reasoning came before its first content only when `reasoning > 0`. With 0 it counts all output over the window from the first content to the end. A reply whose reasoning never streamed then counts those tokens in a window that doesn't hold the time they were written in: the case e6dd5d20 and #1463 stop for gateway rows.\n\nIt shows once a Pi row has a first-token time. Stock Pi writes no `message.ttft` (`piCallLine` reads it as omp's), so its rows show no speed. A Pi extension that writes `ttft` on each assistant message (ms from `message.timestamp` to the first text, thinking or tool-call delta) gives them one. omp writes `ttft` itself; I haven't checked whether it writes `usage.reasoning`.\n\n## Example\n\ngemini-3.8-flash-high (effort high) through a Chat-compatible proxy, one assistant message from the Pi session file, content shortened:\n\n```json\n{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"toolCall\"}],\"durationMs\":7594,\"ttft\":7360,\n \"usage\":{\"input\":3327,\"output\":300,\"cacheRead\":41350,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"reasoning\":151}}\n```\n\nNo thinking block reached Pi; the reply is one tool call. magpie's request list shows 1,282 tok/s: 300 / (7594 − 7360) ms. The 151 reasoning tokens were written inside the 7,360 ms before the tool call came. The 234 ms window is over `MinDecodeMs` and 1,282 tok/s is under `MaxDecodeSpeed`, so #731's bounds don't catch it.\n\nRead with reasoning 151, `DecodeOf` has no first text and no visible-reasoning evidence for this row and shows no speed.\n\n## Fix\n\n`piUsage` takes `reasoning`, and `piCall` sets `c.Reasoning` from it. Pi's `output` already includes it, as Codex's does, so `Tokens` is unchanged.\n\nSeen on main at 45593cc1d.\n",
