   "updated_at": "2026-10-22T20:17:00Z",
   "body": "Implemented in my fork: [b506ff5](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/b506ff5), branch [`fix/pi-reasoning-usage`](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/pi-reasoning-usage).\n\n`piUsage` now reads `usage.reasoning`, and `piCall` keeps it in the request record. Output totals are unchanged: pi-ai explicitly defines reasoning as a subset of output. The existing hidden-reasoning decode guard can therefore suppress the misleading speed for the reported 151-reasoning/300-output call. Both Pi and omp use this reader. Request cache v16 rebuilds older cached rows, including unchanged session files.\n\nRegression: the reported assistant-message shape fails on the old parser for both agents (reasoning 0 instead of 151); missing and zero reasoning keep their previous behavior. `TestPiCalls*` passes with Go 1.26.8, `-race -count=3`.\n\nIntegrated with the other fork fixes at [3833e3f3](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/3833e3f36e37ee851d78b033cd8b27fb7e14dd5a): native/Linux nogui/Windows vet and builds, plus the full `go test -tags nogui ./... -count=1 -timeout=45m`, all pass under an isolated HOME and umask 027.\n\nNot checked against a real Pi/omp session or vendor account; the regression uses the message shape in this report. No upstream PR opened.\n",
